WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.721
A composition feeds one function's output into another

00:00:03.721 --> 00:00:09.118
First x becomes two x plus three; then that entire result is squared

00:00:09.118 --> 00:00:14.100
A change in x therefore passes through two layers before changing y.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.880
The outer derivative is two u, but it measures change per unit of u

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.969
Multiply by the inner derivative, two, to measure change per unit of x

00:00:25.969 --> 00:00:29.100
At zero the resulting tangent slope is twelve.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.206
Now use a square root outside four plus x squared

00:00:34.206 --> 00:00:40.294
Its derivative is one over twice the square root, multiplied by two x from the inside

00:00:40.294 --> 00:00:44.100
Cancelling the constant two gives x over the square root.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.873
The chain rule keeps the original function's domain

00:00:48.873 --> 00:00:54.951
For the natural logarithm of two x plus three, the inside must be positive

00:00:54.951 --> 00:01:03.200
The derivative formula alone also accepts some negative denominators, but those inputs never belonged to the original real function.
